      "math_academy_id": "q-329266",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+2{e}^{3t} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,x(t)+{e}^{3t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-5}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-6}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-1)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{3t}\\cdot 2 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+0\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{3t}\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$",
